Description: Add support for building against Linux 7.3 kernels
 The following kernel interface changes are handled:
  - the legacy ACPI bus driver interface (struct acpi_driver and
    acpi_bus_register_driver()) is gone; fall back to the no-op ACPI
    implementation when it is unavailable;
  - strncpy() was removed, use equivalent bounded copies instead;
  - the global screen_info variable is gone, report no framebuffer;
  - the per-VMA lock was reworked (VM_REFCNT_EXCLUDE_READERS_FLAG),
    implement vma_start_write() without depending on GPL-only symbols;
  - DRM renamed struct drm_atomic_state to struct drm_atomic_commit and
    changed the plane/crtc atomic_check and swap_state callbacks;
  - dma_fence_signal() now returns void.
 All changes are guarded by conftests so that older kernels keep using
 the existing code paths.

